<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!--
        No-op on 19.0.

        On 18.0 this file replaced l10n_ca.pst_external_layout's <li>
        with a clean "GST/HST: <vat>" + "PST: <pst>" pair, and added a
        matching GST line to the folder layout. Both fixes are now
        redundant in 19.0:

        - l10n_ca.pst_external_layout in 19 contains only the PST <li>
          (the GST line was dropped from that template).
        - The upstream web.external_layout_* templates render
          "<country.vat_label>: <vat>" inside company_address_list, and
          for Canada vat_label = "GST/HST number" — so the GST line is
          already there exactly once.

        Keeping our old override would replace the correct upstream PST
        line with our own copy AND emit a duplicate "GST/HST" line right
        next to the upstream "GST/HST number" line. That's the bug
        reported on the first 19.0 invoice preview. Stub left in place
        so the module remains installable for forward-compat.
    -->
</odoo>
